{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jer-29-1","title":"Jeremiah 29:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Jeremiah sends a letter to the captives in Babylon to be quiet there, 8 and not to believe the dreams of their prophets; 10 and that they shall return with grace after seventy years. 15 He foretells the destruction of the rest for their disobedience. 20 He shews the fearful end of Ahab and Zedekiah, two lying prophets. 24 Shemaiah writes a letter against Jeremiah. 30 Jeremiah foretells his doom.</p>\n<p>Cir. A.M. 3407. B.C. 597. Now.This transaction is supposed to have taken place in the first or second year of Zedekiah.</p>\n<p>of the letter. 25-29; 2Ch 30:1-6; Es 9:20; Ac 15:23; 2Co 7:8; Ga 6:11; Heb 13:22 Re 2:1-3:22 the elders. 24:1-7; 28:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-2","title":"Jeremiah 29:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Jeconiah. 22:24-28 Coniah. 27:20; 28:4; 2Ki 24:12-16; 2Ch 36:9,10 Jehoiachin. eunuchs. or, chamberlains. 2Ki 9:32; *marg: 2Ki 20:18; Da 1:3-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-3","title":"Jeremiah 29:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Shaphan. 26:24; 39:14; 2Ki 22:8; Eze 8:11 Gemariah. 36:25; 2Ki 22:12; 2Ch 34:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-4","title":"Jeremiah 29:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>whom. 24:5; Isa 5:5; 10:5,6; 45:7; 59:1,2; Am 3:6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-5","title":"Jeremiah 29:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>10,28; Eze 28:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-6","title":"Jeremiah 29:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Take ye. 16:2-4; Ge 1:27,28; 9:7; 1Ti 5:14 take wives. Ge 21:21; 24:3,4,51,60; 28:1-4; 29:19; 34:4; Jud 1:12-14; 12:9; 14:2 1Co 7:36-38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-7","title":"Jeremiah 29:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>seek. Da 4:27; 6:4,5; Ro 13:1,5; 1Pe 2:13-17 pray. Ezr 6:10; 7:23; Da 4:19; 1Ti 2:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-8","title":"Jeremiah 29:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Let. 14:14; 23:21; 27:14,15; 28:15; Zec 13:4; Mt 24:4,5,24 Mr 13:5,6,22,23; Lu 21:8; Ro 16:18; 2Co 11:13-15; Eph 4:14; 5:6 2Th 2:3,9-11; 2Ti 3:13; 2Jo 1:7-9; Re 13:14; 19:20 your dreams. 5:31; Mic 2:11; Lu 6:26; 2Pe 2:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-9","title":"Jeremiah 29:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>falsely. Heb. in a lie. 23,31; 27:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-10","title":"Jeremiah 29:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>after. 25:12; 27:7,22; 2Ch 36:21-23; Ezr 1:1,2; Da 9:2; Zec 7:5 I will. 24:6,7; 32:42-44; Zep 2:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-11","title":"Jeremiah 29:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>I know. Job 23:13; Ps 33:11; 40:5; Isa 46:10,11; 55:8-12; Mic 4:12; Zec 1:6 Zec 8:14,15 thoughts. 3:12-19; 30:18-22; 31:1-33:26; Isa 40:1-46:13; Eze 34:11-31 Eze 36:1-37:28; 39:1-29; Ho 2:14-23; 3:5; 14:2-9; Joe 2:28-32 Am 9:8-15; Mic 5:4-7; 7:14-20; Zep 3:14-20; Zec 9:9-17; 12:5-10 Zec 14:20,21; Re 14:8-14 expected end. Heb. end and expectation. La 3:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-12","title":"Jeremiah 29:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>31:9; 33:3; Ne 2:4-20; Ps 10:17; 50:15; 102:16,17; Isa 30:19; 65:24 Eze 36:37; Da 9:3-19; Zec 13:9; Mt 7:7,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-13","title":"Jeremiah 29:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>ye shall. Le 26:40-45; De 4:29-31; 30:1-20; 1Ki 8:47-50; 2Ch 6:37-39 Ps 91:15; Isa 55:6,7; Ho 5:15; 6:1-3; Am 5:4-6; Zep 2:1-3 Lu 11:9,10 with. 3:10; 24:7; De 30:2,10; 1Ki 2:4; 2Ki 23:3; 2Ch 22:9; 31:21 Ps 119:2,10,58,69,145; Joe 2:12; Ac 8:37</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-14","title":"Jeremiah 29:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>I will be. De 4:7; 1Ch 28:9; 2Ch 15:12-15; Ps 32:6; 46:1; Isa 45:19; 55:6 Ro 10:20 and I will turn. 16:14,15; 23:3-8; 24:5-7; 30:3,10; 31:8-14; 32:37-44; 33:7-26 Jer 46:27,28; 50:4,5,19,20,33,34; 51:10; Ps 126:1,4; Eze 11:16-20 Eze 34:1-31; 36:1-39:29; Am 9:14; Mic 4:12; Zep 3:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-15","title":"Jeremiah 29:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>8,9; 28:1-17; Eze 1:1,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-16","title":"Jeremiah 29:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>3; 24:2; 38:2,3,17-23; Eze 6:1-9:11; 17:12-21; 21:9-27; 22:31 Eze 24:1-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-17","title":"Jeremiah 29:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>Behold. 18; 15:2,3; 24:8-10; 34:17-22; 43:11; 52:6; Eze 5:12-17; 14:12-21 Lu 21:11,23 them like. 24:1-3,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-18","title":"Jeremiah 29:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>will deliver. 15:4; 24:9; 34:17; Le 26:33; De 28:25,64; 2Ch 29:8; Ps 44:11 Eze 6:8; 12:15; 22:15; 36:19; Am 9:9; Zec 7:14; Lu 21:24 to be a curse. Heb. for a curse. 22; 19:8; 25:9; 26:6; 42:18; De 29:21-28; 1Ki 9:7,8; 2Ch 7:19-22; 29:8 Isa 65:15; La 2:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-19","title":"Jeremiah 29:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>6:19; 7:13,24-26; 25:3-7; 26:5; 32:33; 34:17; 35:14-16; 44:4,5 Zec 1:4-6; 7:11-13; Heb 12:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-20","title":"Jeremiah 29:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>hear.Dr. Blayney thinks there were two letters written by the prophet to the captives in Babylon, and the first ends with this verse. That having heard, on the return of the embassy, that the captives had received his advices favourably, and because they were deceived by false prophets, who promised them a speedier deliverance, he therefore wrote a second letter, beginning with the fifteenth verse, and going on with the twenty-first, etc. (in which order these verses are read in the Septuagint,) in which he denounces God's judgments on the three chief of those, Ahab, Zedekiah, and Shemaiah.</p>\n<p>all ye. Eze 3:11,15 whom. 24:5; Mic 4:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-21","title":"Jeremiah 29:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>which. 8,9; 14:14,15; La 2:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-22","title":"Jeremiah 29:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>shall be. Ge 48:20; Ru 4:11; Isa 65:15; 1Co 16:22 roasted. Da 3:6,21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-23","title":"Jeremiah 29:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>and have. 7:9,10; 23:14,21; Ps 50:16-18; Zep 3:4; 2Pe 2:10-19; Jude 1:8-11 lying. 8,9,21 even I. 13:27; 16:17; 23:23,24; Pr 5:21; Mal 2:14; 3:5; Heb 4:13; Re 1:5 Re 3:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-24","title":"Jeremiah 29:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>Shemaiah. 31,32 Nehelamite. or, dreamer. 8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-25","title":"Jeremiah 29:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>Because. 1Ki 21:8-13; 2Ki 10:1-7; 19:9,14; 2Ch 32:17; Ezr 4:7-16; Ne 6:5,17 Ne 6:19; Ac 9:2 Zephaniah. 29; 21:1,2; 37:3; 52:24; 2Ki 25:18-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-26","title":"Jeremiah 29:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>officers. 20:1,2; 2Ki 11:15,18; Ac 4:1; 5:24 for every. 2Ki 9:11; Ho 9:7; Mr 3:21; Joh 10:20; Ac 26:11,24; 2Co 5:13-15 and maketh. 27; De 13:1-5; Zec 13:3-6; Mt 21:23; Joh 8:53; 10:33 that thou. 20:1,2; 38:6,28; 2Ch 16:10; 18:26; Ac 5:18; 16:24; 2Co 11:33; Re 2:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-27","title":"Jeremiah 29:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>therefore. 2Ch 25:16; Am 7:12,13; Joh 11:47-53; Ac 4:17-21; 5:28,40 which. 26; 43:2,3; Nu 16:3; Mt 27:63; 2Ti 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-28","title":"Jeremiah 29:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>1-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-31","title":"Jeremiah 29:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>Send. 20 Because. 9,23; 14:14,15; 23:21; 28:15-17; Eze 13:8-16,22,23; 2Pe 2:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jer-29-32","title":"Jeremiah 29:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JER","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>punish. 20:6; Ex 20:5; Nu 16:27-33; Jos 7:24,25; 2Ki 5:27; Ps 109:8-15 Isa 14:20,22; Am 7:17 he shall. 22:30; 35:19; 1Sa 2:30-34 behold. 10-14; 17:6; 2Ki 7:2,19,20 rebellion. Heb. revolt. 28:16; *marg:</p>"}]}